────────────────────────────────────────
PLANS, USAGE LIMITS, BILLING (J1/J2)
────────────────────────────────────────

Plan fundamentals:
- Plan determines features and limits (featuresJson or dedicated fields).
- Price can be overridden per workspace via Subscription priceOverride fields.
- Price overrides MUST NOT change features or limits.

One workspace = one subscription:
- Enforce exactly one Subscription per Tenant (recommended via unique tenantId).

Usage counters:
- Use TenantUsageMonthly (tenantId, yearMonth) to track:
  - requestsCreated
  - exportsGenerated
- Counters increment ONLY on successful actions.
- Counter increments must be atomic (single DB transaction / safe update).

Gating rules (hard block):
- Before creating a request:
  - validate plan is active
  - validate requestsCreated < limit (unless unlimited)
- Before exporting:
  - validate exportsGenerated < limit (unless unlimited)
- If limit exceeded:
  - return HTTP 402/403 (choose a standard) with code "UPGRADE_REQUIRED"
  - do not partially mutate anything

Recommended shared helpers:
- resolveTenantPlan(tenantId) -> { planCode, limits, flags }
- assertWithinPlanLimit(tenantId, actionType) -> throws typed error

Plan changes:
- Upgrades apply immediately.
- Downgrades do not delete data; they block new actions beyond limits.
- Plan changes should be auditable (see AuditLog rules).

Pricing overrides:
- Store optional fields on Subscription (e.g. priceOverrideMonthly, discountNote, discountEndsAt).
- If override is set, UI should display that as "Your negotiated price" (optional).
